{
  "rationale": "Evidence: all 60 development trials across oval, s-bend and slalom ended off_track with zero completions, and max_error sits at about 0.061 m on every track. That is the off-track limit (max(0.06, 0.0125 + 0.12/4)), so the robot leaves the tape by a consistent overshoot, not slow drift. Iteration 1 was best (49.4), with oval progress 0.20. Iteration 2 lowered kp and speed and moved the sensors forward to y=0.05. Oval progress fell to 0.11 and s-bend and slalom were unchanged. So the controller was under-correcting rather than over-driven, and the y=0.05 change looks harmful. Iteration 2 also lowered kd, and steering oscillation dropped, but that was not enough to keep the robot on the line. Changes from iteration 1: (1) kp 4.0 to 5.5 for a stronger correction per unit of offset on the sharp bends where the robot exits; (2) kd held at 0.5 (not raised further) because kd 0.5 with kp 4 gave better tracking than kd 0.2 with kp 3, and the oscillation penalty is small compared with leaving the track; (3) ki 0.2 added to cancel the fixed left/right motor mismatch, which causes a steady drift that the proportional term alone leaves as offset; integral is capped at ±2 so windup is limited; (4) sensor y reverted to 0.03 (iteration 1 value), since y=0.05 reduced oval progress; (5) base_speed kept at 1.4, so the speed-versus-control change is isolated to kp, ki and kd. Geometry otherwise matches iteration 1: 16 mm sensors spread ±0.06 m, wheel_track 0.14, mass 0.6. Expected result: fewer off-track exits, max_error below 0.05 on s-bend and slalom, and progress above 0.25 on oval. Hypotheses to check next: (H1) if steering_oscillation rises above about 0.2 with max_error unchanged, kp is too high and kd must rise to damp it; (H2) if the robot now survives but progress stalls at similar values, the limit is speed and base_speed should rise to about 1.6 to reach the 1.5 m/s finish rate; (H3) if ki causes drift or a slow wobble, ki should go to 0. Measurements wanted: completion, progress, completion_time, rms_error, max_error, line_loss_events, steering_oscillation, control_effort and noise_robustness per track.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.06, "y": 0.03},
      {"x": -0.03, "y": 0.03},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.03},
      {"x": 0.03, "y": 0.03},
      {"x": 0.06, "y": 0.03}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.016,
    "wheel_track": 0.14,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.18,
    "mass": 0.6
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.4,
    "kp": 5.5,
    "ki": 0.2,
    "kd": 0.5,
    "sensor_weights": [-1.0, -0.5, 0.0, 0.5, 1.0],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": [
      "completion",
      "progress",
      "completion_time",
      "rms_error",
      "max_error",
      "line_loss_events",
      "steering_oscillation",
      "control_effort",
      "noise_robustness"
    ]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Stronger kp, small ki",
      "notes": "Raises kp from 4.0 to 5.5 and adds ki 0.2 to cancel the fixed motor mismatch, keeping the iteration-1 geometry and kd 0.5. Based on iteration 1 being best and iteration 2 (lower kp, y=0.05) losing oval progress, the robot appears to under-correct on bends."
    }
  }
}
